notes.M01.guidance.push('Product routes now check X-App-Platform (android or ios) and X-App-Build against the current persisted release policy. While both minimum builds are 1, absent headers remain accepted for existing development clients. Once staff confirm a store URL and raise either minimum above 1, both headers are required on product routes; malformed/missing headers return 400 invalid-app-build/app-build-required, and an obsolete build returns 426 update-required. On 426, call bootstrap with the same platform/build to show the store URL and stop product requests. Bootstrap, public help/legal, auth, reports/support, account safety/privacy and deletion routes remain reachable. The gate reads current policy for each product request; invalid/missing policy returns 503 release-policy-unavailable. This does not itself publish an app or verify store availability.');
notes.M02.guidance.push('Local development shortcut: with NODE_ENV=development and OTP_MODE=development, request a sign-in code for +919000000001, then verify with 000000. This is the only fixed pair, and it works only for normal sign-in after a fresh request. The usual ten-minute expiry, one-use rule, five-attempt limit and resend limits still apply. Privacy and phone-change challenges, and every other phone number, use random codes printed only in the local terminal. The fixed pair is unavailable in production and proves no phone ownership. Never put it in a released app.');
notes.M01.status='Implemented lifecycle/reference core, waitlist enrollment, conditional update gate and nonpublic India area administration. Public rollout and outbound waitlist delivery remain pending.';
notes.M01.guidance.push('City operations staff with recent SSO/MFA and city_ops role can GET /admin/v1/areas and PATCH /admin/v1/areas/{id}. List includes prospect areas and versioned state. PATCH requires expectedVersion, state and reasonCode; stale edits return 409 area-version-conflict. Only prospect, seeding, waitlist and gated are writable. soft_launch/open and other countries cannot be enabled through this API. Same-state writes keep the version. A move away from seeding changes public selectability and live readiness; clients must refresh /app/areas and onboarding. Moving out of seeding resets affected dog publication to draft and cancels beacons; live discovery also checks the current state. Returning to seeding never republishes a dog automatically.');
notes.M01.steps.push('City ops: list and review areas','Save nonpublic rollout state','Refresh version and public area list');
notes.M01.screen.push('Staff: state [ waitlist v ]','Reason code [ capacity_pause ]','[ Save area state ]');
notes.M01.examples.push({title:'Pause a development area',request:'PATCH /admin/v1/areas/01920000-0000-7000-8000-0000000e0001',body:{expectedVersion:1,state:'waitlist',reasonCode:'capacity_pause'},response:{id:'01920000-0000-7000-8000-0000000e0001',name:'Bengaluru',countryCode:'IN',adminRegion:'KA',timezone:'Asia/Kolkata',state:'waitlist',version:2,updatedAt:'2026-10-10T10:00:00.000Z'}});
